    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using a difference of squares, \\[ \\begin{gathered} x^4+4=(x^2+2)^2-(2x)^2\\\\ =(x^2-2x+2)(x^2+2x+2). \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Add and subtract \\(4x^2\\) to create a difference of squares",
        "Write \\(x^4+4=(x^2+2)^2-(2x)^2\\)"
      ],
